<title>USA: Clinton clears disaster aid for Florida.</title>
<headline>Clinton clears disaster aid for Florida.</headline>
<dateline>ALBUQUERQUE, N.M. 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Clinton Tuesday declared 16 counties in Florida federal disaster areas following flooding and wind damage caused by Tropical Storm Josephine earlier this month.</p>
<p>The declaration makes victims of the storm eligible for federal assistance and and low-cost loans.</p>
<p>The counties are Baker, Citrus, Clay, Dixie, Duval, Hernando, Hillsborough, Levy, Manatee, Nassau, Pasco, Pinellas, Putnam, Sarasota, Taylor and Volusia.</p>
